{"type":"npc","name":"Braincase","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":235,"temp":0,"max":235,"details":""},"ac":{"value":33,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":0,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":60}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"sleep","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"mental","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"physical","value":10,"exceptions":["adamantine"],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["aetheran","aklo","common"],"details":""},"level":{"value":13},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Braincases are the survivors of a long-lost ritual devised by people who sought to master elemental force by transcending their bodies. Practitioners of the rite are undaunted by the grotesque transformation into a floating brain inside a transparent cranium; instead, they pity those who must dedicate their time to activities like eating and sleeping.</p><p>Braincases are cunning, domineering, and egotistical. They are rarely willing to go along with anyone else's ideas. Though they prefer to avoid the risks of combat against creatures whose strength approaches their own, once battle begins, they seldom surrender until their brain is exposed.</p><h2>Brain Trusts</h2><p>Braincases generally lack the patience required to work with others, but when the opinions of two or more braincases align, they may join together to form a braintrust. Thankfully, a braintrust is usually short-lived, disbanding as soon as its members discover even the slightest difference of opinion. Until then, the effectiveness of multiple braincases working together can be truly terrifying.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 375/840/1,560 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> armor (light, medium), shield, perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Arcana, Deception, Intimidation, Occultism, Society)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> ban